| !Run for !TORCS (The Open Racing Car Simulator, RISC OS port)
| Lines starting with | are comments.
Set TORCS$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <TORCS$Dir>.!Sprites

| The program is an Absolute file with UnixLib inside it, but it needs
| UnixLib's SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (both from PackMan).
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error TORCS needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error TORCS needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
| UnixLib's thread timer module: the sound (OpenAL) runs in a thread. It
| must be loaded before the program starts.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.03 RMLoad <TORCS$Dir>.PThrTicker
| Sound (OpenAL through SDL) goes through SharedSoundBuffer, StreamManager
| and SharedSound (in !System), mixed with other programs' sound.
| SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager are in ssb.zip from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html. Without them
| TORCS plays silently.
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer
| A hardware overlay can show the picture (*Set EGL$Overlay on): load
| ROOL's VideoOverlay module if it's there. TORCS runs without it.
RMEnsure VideoOverlay 0.00 IfThere System:Modules.VideoOverlay Then RMLoad System:Modules.VideoOverlay

| Messages go to this file (printing from a desktop program would open a
| command window). The |< keeps <Wimp$ScrapDir> for UnixLib to expand.
| Put a | in front of the Set line to turn the log off.
Set TORCS$Log /|<Wimp$ScrapDir>/TORCSLog

| Settings are kept in <Choices$Write>.TORCS. The race data and the
| robots are in this application.
| Options for the program (take the | off the Set line to use them):
|   -M   multitexturing on (slower with software OpenGL)
Unset TORCS$Options
| Set TORCS$Options -M

| The program (about 20 MB) is loaded into the slot; its heap goes in
| dynamic areas ("TORCS Heap").
WimpSlot -min 24576K -max 24576K
| Do: Run doesn't expand <variables> in its arguments.
Do Run <TORCS$Dir>.!RunImage <TORCS$Options>
